  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "gFSxteX5RLar7QJ4w3rZJsV+rws=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:42.243Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Bankdata is a member-owned Danish cooperative that builds bespoke systems for the banks that own it. Bespoke build would normally be a qualifying signal \u2014 no product of its own to protect \u2014 but here it is an in-house service to the owners rather than an offer made in a market.\n\nThe consequence is that Bankdata cannot function as a channel. It does not sell delivery to third parties, so there is no route through it to other buyers; any engagement would be with the owner-banks' own systems, which makes it a direct-adoption target and a slow one. Its stack was not researched, and it sits at priority 4 behind an open-source screen.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**4 \u00b7 needs OSS screen**\n- Bankdata (DK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> MEMBER-OWNED COOPERATIVE. Builds bespoke systems for the banks that own it.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:29:42.243158Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:29:42.243162Z"
    }
  },
